    "justification": "Clear at 902: one point above the highest-scoring fraud the scorecard is expected to stop before money moves (901). 3 fraud persona(s) in post-purchase classes (F05) were excluded from this boundary, scoring as high as 970. The taxonomy assigns them to the fulfillment oracle and the payout rather than to a pillar, because a merchant that intends not to ship looks exactly like one that intends to. Including them would have set Clear at 971 and put the established honest merchants outside it, which would make the band mean \"nothing bad can ever happen\". That is not a claim an underwriter can make, and it is what the bond answers instead. Decline floor at 725: the lowest-scoring known-honest merchant, so no merchant we believe honest is declined outright. Conditional at 800: the point of maximum separation inside the overlap region, Youden's J of 0.675 across 39 merchants. The overlap spans 725 to 970 and is where a human label is worth most, which is why it is the refer band."
