  "caveat": "This set validates RANKING, not absolute probability. Roughly 40 to 60 self-authored personas can demonstrate that the scorecard orders merchants correctly and that frauds concentrate in the low bands. They cannot calibrate a price, and a band holding three merchants produces an estimate whose error bar covers the entire pricing range. PD(score) is therefore a stated prior taken from published card-industry fraud rates by band, not a curve fitted to this set. Real calibration would take label counts in the tens of thousands with observed outcomes, not authored intent."
